* Sat Oct 24 2026 Thomas Sappl <thomas.sappl@gmail.com> - 1.3.0-1
- Share target: share a link from the browser (or text with an address)
  to "Sailfeed – Subscribe to website"; Sailfeed opens, also when closed,
  and finds the site's feeds.
- Subscribe to website: feeds that carry the same articles as a subscribed
  feed are marked "Probably already subscribed", also under another
  address or name; an address copied without https:// is taken from the
  clipboard.
- Reader mode: short articles (e.g. OSnews link posts) are shown instead
  of the site's footer.
- German: the swipe tip uses the same "du" form as the other tips.

* Mon Oct 19 2026 Thomas Sappl <thomas.sappl@gmail.com> - 1.2.0-1
- Feed settings: long press a feed → "Feed settings …", or "Feed settings"
  in the pulley of a feed's article list. Name and folder (rename and move
  moved here), and the feed's own list view, preview (show or skip) and
  full article mode (reader mode, original website, browser) – each like
  the general setting until changed; reset of the feed's text size; the
  feed's address (tap to copy).
- Compact list view: title and source only, small thumbnail, about twice
  as many articles per page (Settings → Article list, also per feed).
- Order of the article list: newest first or oldest first.
- Articles without text in the feed (e.g. news.ORF.at) open the full
  article directly instead of an empty preview.
- Reader mode: swipe left for the next article (swipe right still goes
  back); a one-time tip shows it.
- Slow connections: the reader mode keeps waiting while the page still
  arrives instead of starting over; after 10 s it offers the text from the
  feed or the browser; no more blank page with busy indicators.
- Storage: read articles older than 1, 3, 6 or 12 months are deleted at
  the start (bookmarks and unread articles always stay; new installations
  3 months, updates "Never" with a one-time hint); number of articles and
  database size in the settings. Image cache size adjustable (50–500 MB)
  and "Clear image cache".
- The new settings are part of the settings backup.

* Thu Oct 15 2026 Thomas Sappl <thomas.sappl@gmail.com> - 1.1.0-1
- Subscribe to website: enter (or paste) the address of a website, an
  article or a feed; Sailfeed finds the site's feeds (announced in the
  page, linked, in parent pages or at well-known addresses of common blog
  systems), checks them and shows each with its newest articles to
  subscribe, into a folder. Comment feeds and podcasts are marked.
- Search ("Search" in the pulley of the article list and the feed list) in
  the articles on the device – titles, or titles and text, in all feeds or
  the current selection, read ones included – and in feed titles.
- Web view pulley: "Subscribe to website" for the page shown, e.g. a blog
  linked in an article.
- First start: the sign-in page explains Nextcloud News (with links),
  empty article and feed lists say how to subscribe; tips for the hidden
  gestures (feed list, full article, pulley, mark-all button, long press),
  one at a time; press and hold the icon in About to see them again.
- New app icon.
- Links in articles open in reader mode inside the app or in the browser
  (setting); a long press opens them the other way. Links with
  target="_blank" work now. A link opens as its own page with a back
  button.
- Previous/next article slides in from the matching side.
- Reader mode appears without the original page flashing up.
- Article list: room below the camera when paging, paging needs a shorter
  swipe, no highlight when a swipe starts.
- Article list: "Show read articles" / "Load older articles" always in the
  same place; no wrong "No older articles" hint.
- Articles at the end of the list are marked as read reliably.
- Settings reorganised: a short main page with a summary per subject and
  the settings on sub-pages (article list, article preview, reader mode,
  Nextcloud account and backup, privacy); live preview for text sizes,
  font, spacing, margins and colours that stays in view in the reader mode
  settings; mark-as-read delay as a choice.
- Fix: choices in the settings (links in articles, font, colours, line
  spacing, margins, full article, greying out, feed sort order) could
  change by themselves when the settings page opened.
- Reader mode: the bottom bar switches between reader mode and original
  website; "Open in browser", "Share", "Copy link" and "Subscribe to
  website" in a shorter pulley.
- Article preview: a calm "Show full article" row instead of two buttons;
  share, copy link and open in browser in the pulley.
- Fix: large gap below the title of articles that start with an image.
- Subscribe to website: feeds already subscribed are recognised more
  reliably (redirects, the feed's own address, tracking parameters).
- Bottom bar readable in light ambiences (opaque, stronger counter).
- Fix: English texts with "(s)" plurals.

* Sat Oct 10 2026 Thomas Sappl <thomas.sappl@gmail.com> - 1.0.0-1
- First public release (GitHub, OpenRepos).
- Article list with thumbnails and excerpts, grouped by day, page-wise
  scrolling, read articles greyed out, unread dot; optionally unread only,
  with read and older articles on request.
- Feed list with bookmarks, folders (also empty ones), favicons and unread
  counts; sort by unread, name or activity; favorite feeds; feeds without
  folder selectable as "Other feeds".
- Feed management: add feeds and folders, rename, move, delete.
- Automatic mark as read (when scrolling on or at once), push-up button to
  mark all as read, context menus (read/unread, bookmark, above/below, feed,
  folder), all with undo.
- Reader mode (Mozilla Readability) with preloading, consent wall handling
  with the in-app browser's cookies, font, text size (also per feed), line
  spacing, margins, colors (light/dark/sepia), images, sites that always
  open in the original; links open in reader mode or in the browser
  (setting, long press the other way).
- Full article in reader mode, as the original website or in the browser;
  the preview can be skipped.
- Bar in preview and reader mode: previous/next, text size, bookmark,
  open in browser; swipe gestures between list, preview and reader.
- Portrait and landscape.
- Sign-in with the browser (Nextcloud Login Flow v2) or an app password,
  self-signed certificates, understandable error hints and an error banner.
- Settings backup in your own Nextcloud files: automatic after changes,
  earlier states kept, restore (replace or add missing only) with undo,
  offered after signing in on a new device.
- Privacy settings for the in-app browser's cookies and website data.
- English and German.
